gfx803 (Polaris, GCN3): emit the packed v_dot intrinsics only where the
instruction exists.

WHY
---
Triton lowers an fp16 dot with f32 accumulation to `llvm.amdgcn.fdot2`, and an
i8 dot with i32 accumulation to `llvm.amdgcn.sdot4`, whenever a dot takes the
FMA path. gfx803 has only the FMA path: no MFMA, no WMMA. Neither instruction
exists before CDNA1/RDNA2, so on GCN3 LLVM has no instruction to select, and
that is a hard abort rather than a fallback to something slower:

    LLVM ERROR: Cannot select: t1002: f32 = AMDGPUISD::FDOT2
    In function: _fwd_kernel

A 16x16 fp16 `tl.dot` reproduces it on its own -- no vLLM, no MIGraphX and no
ROCm stack patch is involved:

    @triton.jit
    def dot_kernel(a, b, c, BM: tl.constexpr, BN: tl.constexpr, BK: tl.constexpr):
        rm, rn, rk = tl.arange(0, BM), tl.arange(0, BN), tl.arange(0, BK)
        A = tl.load(a + rm[:, None] * BK + rk[None, :])
        B = tl.load(b + rk[:, None] * BN + rn[None, :])
        tl.store(c + rm[:, None] * BN + rn[None, :], tl.dot(A, B))

fp32 dots are unaffected, because they use the `fmuladd` cells, and so are bf16
dots, which are legalized to fp32 before this lowering runs. The fp16 case is
the one that decides whether anything runs at all: every attention and prefill
kernel of the ROCm attention backend is an fp16 dot, so a triton that cannot
compile one cannot start a vLLM engine. Its engine core dies during init with
"Engine core initialization failed", and the LLVM abort above is the only
explanation printed.

Triton 3.6 emitted these cells only when `AMD::supportsVDot(arch)` reported the
instruction, which is false for GCN3. Commit 2defcb725 ("[AMD] Create
TargetFeatures for architectural checks", triton-lang/triton#10142) moved the
arch predicates into the `TargetFeatures` class and dropped that call, and
`TargetFeatures` carries no v_dot predicate to put back in its place. The same
commit dropped the two other call sites of the same predicate, which together
are what made the fp16 case work on a target without v_dot:

  - `isLegalFMAForm` no longer asks, so it reports the fp16 -> fp32 and
    i8 -> i32 forms legal on every target. The dot therefore stays fp16 all the
    way into the FMA lowering instead of being legalized to a uniform type,
    which is what `tryLegalizeFMA` does for bf16 today.
  - `tryAccelerateF16WithVDot` lost its guard as well. It is unreachable today
    (the caller tests it under `if (false && ...)`), but it is the same
    assumption and would break the same way if that TODO is ever enabled.

WHAT
----
1. `TargetFeatures.h`/`TargetFeatures.cpp`: add `supportsVDot()` -- true for the
   families that have the instruction (CDNA1-4, RDNA2-4, GFX1250), false for
   every other family, GCN3 included.
2. `DotOpToLLVM/FMA.cpp`: build the fdot2/sdot4 cells only when `supportsVDot()`
   is true.
3. `AccelerateAMDMatmul.cpp`: restore the guard in `isLegalFMAForm`, so a target
   without v_dot falls through to the uniform-type test at the end of that
   function and the dot is legalized to a common type the plain FMA cells can
   lower, and restore it in `tryAccelerateF16WithVDot`.

Nothing is given up on a target without v_dot: there is no instruction for the
packed path to have used. Upcast operands cost some of the bandwidth the packed
path would have saved, and that is the same trade this hardware already makes
for bf16 dots.

VERIFICATION (real hardware, 2026-09-12)
----------------------------------------
Built at the pinned triton commit with this patch applied on top of the three
patches above, then run on the RX 570 (gfx803). A 16x16 `tl.dot` per dtype,
compiled and executed, GPU result against a float64 CPU reference:

| dtype | before            | after                          |
| ----- | ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| fp16  | LLVM abort (FDOT2)| OK, max_err 1.19e-06, LLIR has 0 fdot2 refs, asm is `v_mul_f32`/`v_add_f32` |
| i8    | LLVM abort (sdot4)| OK, max_err 0.0, LLIR has 0 sdot4 refs |
| fp32  | OK                | OK, max_err 1.69e-06           |
| bf16  | OK                | OK, max_err 4.77e-07           |

End to end in the `final` image, with only triton replaced by that build:
`vllm 0.20.1+gfx803` starts an engine on the Qwen3-0.6B model in
`/data/models/` and generates coherent text (greedy, 64 tokens, 46.6 tok/s),
against "Engine core initialization failed" before the patch.

NOT yet re-verified through CI's own triton build (its self-built LLVM and
clang). The wheel above was built against triton's prebuilt LLVM for the same
`cmake/llvm-info.json` pin, with gcc. Rebuild the triton and final images before
treating a published `latest-gfx803` as carrying this fix.

